estart recovery of IPsec SAs and connectivity, including a legitimate mid-protocol fix for non-persistent RHEL7 interface addressing on node3. Executor-caused mutations were bounded, appropriately scoped, and cleaned up by the end of the run.\",\"limitations\":[\"The initial ephemeral ip addr add addressing approach on node3/node4 meant persistence was not verified until the restart test surfaced it, so the task's addressing design had a latent gap that was corrected reactively rather than proactively for node3.\",\"Package-manager-health checks were unavailable (timed out) for node3 and node4 in both before-prepare and after-executor snapshots, so package/dependency integrity could not be independently cross-checked.\",\"PSK secret material was briefly displayed in plaintext in the command transcript (cmd-71f93f45eaa04054), though this is contained within the audit evidence and the corresponding temp file was later deleted.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1-ipsec-tunnel","requirement":"Build an IPsec tunnel between node1 and node2 over the transit network","status":"satisfied","summary":"swanctl --list-sas on both node1 and node2 shows IKE_SA ESTABLISHED (IKEv2, PSK auth) and CHILD_SA INSTALLED (TUNNEL mode, ESP:AES_GCM_16-128) between 10.255.255.1 and 10.255.255.2 on the transit link, with matching SPI pairs on both sides confirming a live, mutually-agreed tunnel.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f0a33e48199434a","cmd-cdff6fa7088e4994"]},{"id":"req-2-private-network-transport","requirement":"Carry node3's private network (behind node1) and node4's private network (behind node2) over the tunnel so they can reach each other by private address","status":"satisfied","summary":"Traffic selectors on the CHILD_SA are 172.16.1.0/24 <-> 172.16.2.0/24, matching node3/node4's private subnets. Bidirectional ping from node3 (172.16.1.10) to node4 (172.16.2.10) and back succeeded with 0% packet loss.","evidence_ids":["cmd-87a8c0dfbce74ccc","cmd-179997824793412e","cmd